.TH CBMAP_DESTROY 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cbmap_destroy \- Destroy a CBMap and release its memory

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB cbmap_destroy (cbmap_t* cmap_ptr);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcbmap_destroy\fR function is used to destroy a CBMap and release all associated memory. This function traverses the entire map, deleting each key-value pair, and frees the memory allocated for the map.

The function takes one parameter:
.TP
.B cmap_ptr
A pointer to the pointer of the CBMap to be destroyed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcbmap_destroy\fR function to destroy a CBMap and release its memory:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cbmap_internal.h>

int main() {
    cbmap_t map = cbmap_new();

    // Assume map is initialized and used somewhere

    // Destroy the CBMap and release its memory
    cbmap_destroy(&map);

    return 0;
}
.nef